        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "41d27fe7-0570-500c-a278-1693f9a37cc1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Breeds: Maremma Sheepdog, Austrian Pinscher\n- Places: Italy, central Italy, Abruzzo, Maremma, Tuscany, Lazio, Austria\n- Roles: livestock guardian dog, farm dog, home guard, drover, rat catcher\n- Animals: Arthur, wolves\n- People: Mikael Lindnord\n\nFacts:\n- The Maremma Sheepdog, or Cane da pastore Maremmano-Abruzzese, is a breed of livestock guardian dog indigenous to central Italy, especially Abruzzo and the Maremma region of Tuscany and Lazio.\n- The Maremma Sheepdog has been used for centuries by Italian shepherds to guard sheep from wolves.\n- The Austrian Pinscher, also called Österreichischer Pinscher and listed as FCI No. 64, is a medium-sized pinscher-type dog breed from Austria.\n- In Austria, dogs of the Austrian Pinscher type were originally farm dogs that kept barns free of rats and served as home guards, livestock guardians, and drovers.\n- According to Mikael Lindnord, Arthur is presumed to be a Maremma Sheepdog mix.",
